---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Cozy home decor and gift guides for small spaces, written from a small apartment."
>
	<h1>About Hemidal</h1>

	<p>
		Hemidal is about making small spaces feel warm. Not staged, not magazine
		perfect — warm in the way a room feels when someone actually lives in it and
		has figured out where things go.
	</p>

	<p>
		Most home decor advice quietly assumes you have a spare room, a wall you are
		allowed to drill into, and a budget. This site assumes none of that. The
		posts here are about narrow shelves, rented kitchens, corners that have to do
		three jobs, and the small number of things worth buying when there is no room
		for a fourth.
	</p>

	<h2>What you will find here</h2>

	<ul>
		<li>Coffee station and coffee bar setups that fit in a very small kitchen</li>
		<li>Storage and organization ideas that work in a rental</li>
		<li>Seasonal styling in a warm neutral palette — cream, terracotta, bronze</li>
		<li>Gift guides organised by who you are actually buying for</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>How recommendations work</h2>

	<p>
		Posts on this site contain affiliate links. If you buy through one, I may
		earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. As an Amazon Associate I
		earn from qualifying purchases.
	</p>

	<p>
		What that does not change: nothing gets included because it pays more. Where
		a product has a real drawback — it is too tall, it scratches, it only works
		if your shelf is deep enough — that gets said in the post. A recommendation
		you cannot trust is worth nothing to either of us.
	</p>

	<p>
		Full details on the <a href="/disclosure">disclosure page</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Get in touch</h2>

	<p>
		Questions, corrections, or a product you think belongs here:
		<a href="mailto:hello@example.com">hello@example.com</a>.
	</p>
</Layout>
